              blocks  if  no random bytes are available, and when reading from
              the _u_r_a_n_d_o_m source, it blocks if the entropy pool  has  not  yet
              been  initialized.   If  the GGRRNNDD__NNOONNBBLLOOCCKK flag is set, then ggee‐‐
              ttrraannddoomm() does not block in these cases, but instead immediately
              returns -1 with _e_r_r_n_o set to EEAAGGAAIINN.

