NNOOTTEESS
       For  an  overview  and comparison of the various interfaces that can be
       used to obtain randomness, see rraannddoomm(7).

       Unlike _/_d_e_v_/_r_a_n_d_o_m and _/_d_e_v_/_u_r_a_n_d_o_m, ggeettrraannddoomm() does not  involve  the
       use  of pathnames or file descriptors.  Thus, ggeettrraannddoomm() can be useful
       in cases where cchhrroooott(2) makes _/_d_e_v pathnames invisible, and  where  an
       application  (e.g.,  a daemon during start‐up) closes a file descriptor
       for one of these files that was opened by a library.

