       As of Linux 3.19 the following limits apply:

       •  When reading from the _u_r_a_n_d_o_m source, a maximum of 32Mi‐1  bytes  is
          returned  by a single call to ggeettrraannddoomm() on systems where _i_n_t has a
          size of 32 bits.

       •  When reading from the _r_a_n_d_o_m source, a maximum of 512 bytes  is  re‐
          turned.

